It's the report card and this is the topic of today's dialogue.

30
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:38,760
That's right.

31
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:42,830
Now you may remember, I'm sure pretty much it's standard everywhere in the world.

32
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:49,990
You get a report, a small little report that tells your parents how well or how poorly you are doing in school.

33
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:50,930
That's right.

34
00:01:51,820 --> 00:02:00,160
And then after maybe two or three months, your teacher will write down how she or he thinks that you're performing at school.

35
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:00,310
That's right.

36
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,850
And usually parents have to sign this.

37
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:09,230
They have to say, okay, I see that my child is doing well or that he's doing poorly and then the teacher will know as well.

38
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:14,570
And I think, well, you get report cards in elementary school, in high school and also in university, right?

39
00:02:14,790 --> 00:02:16,610
You do get a report card of some sort.

40
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:17,150
That's right.

41
00:02:17,390 --> 00:02:19,810
Well, in university in America, we call them grades.

42
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,490
We don't really call them a report card.

43
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:29,640
In high school, middle school and elementary school, so before college, we actually have a piece of paper and that's why it's called a card.

44
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:30,520
Yeah, that's right.

45
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:35,400
I think now for universities especially, you just go online and you see your grades.

46
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:36,300
That's right.

47
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,340
It's on the internet.

48
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:44,680
But the important thing about the report card is that it tells a parent and a student what his or her grades are.

49
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:45,460
That's right.

50
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:49,600
So, grades, this is a noun, is basically your score.

51
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:50,630
That's right.

52
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:58,810
So, maybe you took a test and you did very well on your test and you had some homework and you did very well on your homework, so you have a good grade.

53
00:02:59,480 --> 00:02:59,610
That's right.

54
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,530
But if you don't do your homework and you don't do well on your test, you have a bad grade.

55
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,320
That's right.

56
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,390
So, for example, like in the United States, it's over 100 points.

57
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:11,410
So maybe a good grade would be 95 points out of 100.

58
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:14,530
So we call that an A. That's called an A. That's right.

59
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:21,100
Or if you have a bad grade, maybe that's an F, which is 20% or 30%.

60
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:22,440
Right.

61
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,440
Okay.

62
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:34,420
So now, this is where we need to make a difference between the grades that his father was looking for and then the mom says he's in the third grade.

63
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:40,980
So it's very different between having good grades or bad grades and fifth grade or third grade.

64
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,680
All right.

65
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,680
Two different grades.

66
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,680
And we know this is confusing.

67
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,840
I'm going to explain a little bit.

68
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:50,260
Third grade is actually the third year of elementary school.

69
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:50,880
That's right.

70
00:03:51,720 --> 00:04:00,200
So in the American education system, we start in kindergarten and we have first grade, second grade, third grade, all the way up until the end, which is 12th grade.

71
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:00,760
That's right.

72
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:04,900
So it's everything between when you're five years old and when you're 18 years old.

73
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,360
And each year at school is a grade, a level.

74
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:09,420
That's right.

75
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:14,640
And as you said, it's a grade in different parts of the country.

76
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:21,520
I'm not really sure if they call them a grades or they have the same system, but basically, that's what it means in English.

77
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:25,800
You have first grade, third grade, 12th grade, finally, when you graduate.

78
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:26,280
That's right.

79
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,520
So you can say my son is in eighth grade.

80
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,000
That's right.

81
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:31,640
It means he's in his eighth year of school.

82
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:32,640
Right.

83
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,640
Very good.

84
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,340
So that is the difference.

85
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:43,360
And now, we're going to take a look at something that has to do with grades as well, is the marks that you get in your test or in your report card.

86
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:44,840
That's right.

87
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,120
So this might actually help.

88
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:48,540
Remember when we said on your report card, your teacher might write down your grade.

89
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:52,280
That means do you have an A or a B or a C?

90
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,560
Well, another way to call this is a mark.

91
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,680
So he has good marks.

92
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:56,620
He has good grades.

93
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,440
So they're basically the same thing, grades and marks.

94
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:01,140
That's right.

95
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:01,520
They are.

96
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:07,760
And I know that in Britain, I think people more commonly say marks.

97
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:11,490
She got terrible marks at school and her father was angry with her.

98
00:05:12,370 --> 00:05:17,930
But in America, we often say, if you get good grades, I'll buy you sweets.

99
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:19,090
That's right.

100
00:05:19,210 --> 00:05:19,570
Okay.

101
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:21,880
So you get a prize if you get good grades usually.

102
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,880
Well, it depends on your parents.

103
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,010
On your parents.

104
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:24,880
That's right.

105
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:35,700
Now, as we said, you can have a grade that's usually a number or a letter like A, B, C, D, F. But you can also get marks that are just very much black or white.

106
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:39,800
That's satisfactory or unsatisfactory, like in this case.

107
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,800
That's right.

108
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:45,800
So satisfactory, this is an adjective, it describes something, is a good thing.

109
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,280
So how did he do?

110
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,680
Well, his performance was satisfactory.

111
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:51,960
It's okay.

112
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:56,940
But if it's bad or if it's not good, we call it unsatisfactory.

113
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:57,900
That's right.

114
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:01,440
So this doesn't really have a number, as you can tell.

115
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:04,320
It's just basically pass or fail.

116
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,320
That's about it.

117
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:05,920
Good or bad.

118
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:07,320
Good or bad.

119
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:08,320
That's it.

120
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,320
Exactly.

121
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,320
No grade.

122
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,320
And we'll explain this in a minute.

123
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:17,120
There are some classes where you can't have a grade like an A or a B. And that's why we have this satisfactory, unsatisfactory.

124
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:17,280
That's right.

125
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,120
All right.

