162
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:05,980
That's right.

163
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,760
All right.

164
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:16,440
Now talking about one of the subjects in school, that means some of the classes that you have, we had science, we have history, and there's another one called physical education.

165
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,240
All right.

166
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,280
So this is a class that has many different names.

167
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,020
It's physical, so you know that it has to do with your body.

168
00:08:23,790 --> 00:08:29,510
So basically it's sports class and you play sports like football, basketball, things like that.

169
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,640
It's also called PE.

170
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,640
PE for short.

171
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,640
Yeah.

172
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:38,320
Because remember physical in English starts with a P, PH, physical.

173
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:44,320
But this is what I was saying earlier, Marco, you can't give a person an A or a B in physical education.

174
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:44,710
Well, you don't really.

175
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:50,800
So normally students get satisfactory or unsatisfactory.

176
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,970
Because usually it doesn't mean that you have to be very good at sports.

177
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,950
Sometimes it's just the effort counts.

178
00:08:57,240 --> 00:09:07,800
You may not be very good at soccer or football or basketball, but if you try really hard, you're running around and you're actually doing what you're supposed to be doing, then you get a satisfactory note.

179
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:11,960
It means, yeah, I mean, you're not the best player in the world, but you're doing what you're supposed to.

180
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,960
Exactly.

181
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,170
All right.

182
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:21,760
So now when the father was talking, he's like, oh, you know, I don't understand this report card in my day, we got an A or a B.

183
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:22,630
All right.

184
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:28,790
So this is a common phrase that people say when they want to talk about when they were children or when they were growing up.

185
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:34,050
So older people often say, oh, in my day, things were different.

186
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:38,790
So this is a way to make a comparison between now and the past.

187
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:39,510
Yeah, right.

188
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:48,880
So you're basically saying when I was a child or many years ago, this was what happened or this is how it used to be.

189
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,830
In my day, school was much more difficult.

190
00:09:52,230 --> 00:09:54,410
Today, it's very, very easy.

191
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:55,090
That's right.

192
00:09:55,920 --> 00:10:00,930
So this is how you start this comparison between the time when you were a child to now.

193
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,280
Yes.

194
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:02,430
In my day.

195
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:04,280
All right.

196
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:08,720
And to finish off, we're going to talk about failing an exam because obviously sometimes you do fail.

197
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,120
Yeah.

198
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:13,840
So when you fail, fail an exam, you get a very bad grade, an F.

199
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,840
An F.

200
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,840
So F for fail.

201
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,440
It's easy to remember.

202
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,360
That's right.

203
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:23,720
So you say, you can say I didn't pass the exam, but you can also say I failed the exam.

204
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,720
Yes.

205
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:29,640
And normally fail means you received less than 60%.

206
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:30,600
That's right.

207
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:31,840
Or 50%.

208
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,280
So it's, yeah, 50%.

209
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:41,630
So basically you missed, if there are 10 questions on the exam, you missed five or six or seven or all the way to 10 of them.

210
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:44,270
So you missed more than half of the questions.

211
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:44,930
That's right.

212
