I didn't like to pay attention in class, so that was different because I would pay attention, I would take some notes, but then I would just remember everything.

244
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,740
So I did all right for the exam.

245
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:36,200
I didn't really have to study.

246
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,750
But sometimes in other subjects I did, I really liked them.

247
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,880
So it wasn't studying.

248
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:40,790
It was more fun for me.

249
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,270
So then I would get great grades.

250
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:43,450
What about you?

251
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,550
I always studied for tests.

252
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,730
Generally my grades were pretty good.

253
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:52,240
Now something that we didn't talk about here is a GPA.

254
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:55,650
This is something that is very popular in the United States.

255
00:12:56,320 --> 00:13:00,920
Basically even if you want to apply for schools, your GPA is what counts.

256
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:01,340
What is a GPA?

257
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,920
That's right.

258
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:08,040
Well, we don't really have a GPA until high school, and then it's in high school and college.

259
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:13,080
And GPA stands for G-Grade P-Point A-Average.

260
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,260
So grade point average.

261
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:17,800
That means we take all of our marks or all of our grades together.

262
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:22,780
So science grade, English grade, history grade, and we make an average.

263
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:31,240
So if I get mostly A's, my GPA is 4.0.

264
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:34,800
If I get mostly B's, my GPA is 3.0.

265
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,280
And then it goes lower and lower.

266
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:42,270
And if you have a really bad GPA, like a 1, you probably won't finish high school.

267
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:47,040
Now the GPA is very important for many reasons.

268
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:53,840
First of all, because it's also kind of a summary of your application to universities, right?

269
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,100
They take a look at your GPA.

270
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:55,960
Absolutely.

271
00:13:56,020 --> 00:14:01,140
So this is a way to say, okay, how is this student overall?

272
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:06,020
How is this student in all of her classes, not just one class?

273
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:06,460
Right.

274
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:11,120
And then they see if you have a 3.5, they say, oh, well, it's pretty good.

275
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,360
Yeah, 3.5 is good.

276
00:14:12,470 --> 00:14:13,030
4 is the best.

277
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:17,240
And again, a 3 is good, it's okay.

278
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,710
But a 2 or a 1 is not very good.

279
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:19,150
That's right.

280
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:25,040
So it's very interesting because all around the world, they have different grading systems.

281
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:31,870
I think I would say that the United States is the only place where I've seen that they use the A, B, C, D, F system.

282
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:36,890
In Latin American countries, for example, they don't do it over 100, they do it over 10.

283
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:39,480
So you would get a grade over 10.

284
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,310
Or in some countries, over 20.

285
00:14:41,890 --> 00:14:42,470
I've seen that as well.

286
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:43,800
In Italy, it's not.

287
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:44,090
It's over 20.

288
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,800
So you would get a 14, I think, would be a passing grade over 20.

289
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:52,070
Well, let us know, listeners, if you have a different grading system in your country.

290
00:14:52,450 --> 00:14:55,390
Also, you can let us know how were your grades when you're studying in school.

291
00:14:55,870 --> 00:14:58,810
You don't have to tell us, but we'd like to talk to you about grades.

292
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,800
Our website is EnglishPod.com.

293
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:01,450
All right.

294
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:02,090
We'll see you guys there.

295
00:15:02,330 --> 00:15:02,470
Bye.
